  "notes": "HISTORICAL CATALOG YEAR. Built by fetching the real archived 2022-23 bulletin page (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2022-2023/undergraduate/colleges/liberal-arts/communication-arts-sciences-bs/, HTTP 200, raw HTML cross-checked against WebFetch's summary rather than trusted alone), which is a genuinely different curriculum from the 2026 file, not a copy: (1) Total minimum credits is 123, not 120 -- the 2022-23 Program Requirements table itself states General Education 45 + Electives 24 + Requirements for the Major 54 = 123 (vs. 2026's Electives 21 = 120), and the 2022-23 Suggested Academic Plan's own printed semester subtotals (15/15/15/15/15/15/16.5/16.5) sum to exactly 123, confirming the extra 3cr is a genuine 8th-semester elective, not a rounding artifact. (2) The 2025-26/2026-27 'LA 83' (Semester 1) and 'LA 283' Second-Year Liberal Arts Seminar (Semester 4) do not exist in the 2022-23 plan at all -- that college-wide seminar requirement was added to this major's suggested plan sometime between the 2022-23 and 2025-26 editions (confirmed absent in the archived HTML's own semester tables, not simply omitted here). Net effect on the total: 2022-23 has no LA courses (-3cr vs. 2026) but 1 extra elective in the final semester (+3cr vs. 2026), so both years land on 123cr overall -- but the internal composition genuinely differs (different items in Semesters 1/4/8), which is why this is its own file rather than a metadata tweak. (3) The 2022-23 page's own quantification department-list text names 'MATH 18' and 'STAT 470' where the 2023-24 edition onward (and this app's live MATH/STAT catalogs) instead have 'MATH 38' and 'STAT 470W' -- real PSU course renumbering that happened between the 2022-23 and 2023-24 editions. Neither 'MATH 18' nor 'STAT 470' (without the W) exists in Backend/catalogs/math_catalog.json or stat_catalog.json, so both were dropped from this year's quantification pool rather than fabricated as valid picks -- same treatment as the 2026 plan's own precedent of dropping the bulletin-named but catalog-unconfirmed 'STAT 301' (which, per stat_catalog.json, does exist now but is documented as a Behrend-only requirement, not offered at University Park, so still correctly excluded from this UP-scoped plan). Everything else -- the 5 Prescribed courses, the CAS 203/210/215/220 Additional-Course pool, the CAS 4XX/Supporting-CAS match patterns, the Related-Disciplines open elective, and the semester-by-semester course sequence -- is byte-identical to 2023-2026's real requirements, confirmed by diffing this year's fetched Program Requirements and Suggested Academic Plan text against the later years'. CAMPUS: this year's archived page's own 'At which campus can I study this program?' section states Begin Campus: Any Penn State Campus / End Campus: University Park -- same University-Park-only scoping as every other year checked, so no campus expansion applies here either.",
